    description: "WHAT\nTypeScript: a variable declared with a type and no initializer is not typed. let target: ParseBoolPipe; in a describe callback, assigned in beforeEach (target = new ParseBoolPipe()), then target.transform(..) in every it callback: unresolved. Neither the annotation nor the assignment binds the name; only const x = new T() and a typed parameter do.\n\nREPRO\nnest packages/common/test/pipes/parse-bool.pipe.spec.ts lines 6, 8, 13 (~/whole_bunch_of_repos/nest/packages). Line 13's call is unresolved on dev before and after INV-zabud; line 33's was resolved before only because another it callback wrote const target = new ParseBoolPipe(..).\n\nFIX\nBind the annotation of a variable_declarator in the scope that declares it (js_ts.py; var_types is a ScopedVarTypes, so a nested callback sees it). The declaration is evidence, as for a typed parameter.\n\nNOT KNOWN\nHow many calls this types on a real repository."  # c7ee
